# Swift in DeskPetKit

- Port Electron behavior; keep numbers in `Constants`. User-facing copy in `Strings`.
- Inject `DeskPetClock` (and similar) for time; tests use `TestClock`.
- Settings: `Codable` with Electron camelCase keys (`petAppearanceId`). Decode with defaults; `normalized()` on read/write.
- Persistence: `UserDefaults` for settings/position; `stats.json` under Application Support (ADR-4).
- Login: `SMAppService.mainApp` only when `Bundle.main.bundlePath.hasSuffix(".app")`.
- Menus: descriptors in `MenuBuilder`, AppKit in `MenuBuilder.makeMenu`, dispatch `MenuAction` through `AppState.handle`.
- Debug: `DESKPET_DEBUG_*` env vars in `DebugHarness` (`#if DEBUG` only).

```swift
// ❌ BAD — logic in DeskPet executable, or new package
.dependencies: [.package(url: "...")]

// ✅ GOOD — testable type in DeskPetKit, clock injected
public init(clock: DeskPetClock = SystemClock()) { self.clock = clock }
```

Keep types `Sendable`/`Equatable` where they already are. Prefer `enum` namespaces (`DisplayGeometry`, `LoginItemService`) over singleton classes.
